course: dictionary
lesson: 5309
title: Kazak: a people, a language, a rug
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names, and a name can belong to a people, a language or a thing. Kazak is another spelling of Kazakh. The Kazakh people live mainly in Kazakhstan, in Central Asia. Kazak can also work as an adjective, so you can talk about Kazak people or a Kazak rug.
explain: Read the words around it. In «a Kazak rug», the word Kazak tells you what kind of rug it is. A rug is something you put on a floor, so the rug is the thing, and Kazak describes it. A quick check: swap in «a Kazakh rug». It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Check the spelling too. The usual modern spelling for the people is «Kazakh», with an h at the end. You will see both spellings, so do not be surprised. In «"Cossack" came into English from Ukrainian "козак" (kozak) and Russian "kazak"», you can see how one word can travel through several languages and change its spelling on the way.
fact: Kazak is another spelling of Kazakh.
fact: The Kazakh people live mainly in Kazakhstan, in Central Asia.
fact: A Kazak rug is a thick, colourful woollen carpet with bold patterns.
fact: Kazak rugs were first made in the Caucasus region.
fact: Words can come into English from other languages: «"Cossack" came into English from Ukrainian and Russian "kazak"».
exercise: The Kazak people live mainly in which part of the world? | *Central Asia | Central Africa | The Arctic | Northern Scotland
exercise: «a Kazak rug»: what kind of thing is a Kazak rug? | A small bird that lives in mountains | A person from Kazakhstan | A stone used to build walls | *A thick, colourful woollen carpet with bold patterns
exercise: Which is the usual modern spelling for the people? | *Kazakh | Kazuk | Kazock | Kasak
test: Where were Kazak rugs first made? | *The Caucasus region | Central Africa | The Scottish Highlands | Kazakhstan's capital city
test: What part of speech is Kazak in «a Kazak rug»? | *An adjective, describing the rug | A noun, the name of a person | An adverb, telling how | A verb, an action
exam: Which is true of Kazak? | *It is another spelling of Kazakh | It is the name of a bird | It is a kind of mountain | It means very old
